10. AI QUICK-CONTEXT & CODE EXTENSION GUIDANCE
================================================================================
When prompting an AI assistant or extending this project in future tasks, keep the 
following guidelines in mind:

1. Asset References:
   - Always refer to static public files using root absolute paths (e.g., '/heroframes/...', 
     '/Bhaiya.svg', '/heroimage.jpg') or import them from 'src/assets/'.
2. Brand Consistency:
   - Use "Vishwakarma Interior" or "Rishikesh Interior Solutions" for all public-facing 
     titles and branding. Do not use "Atelier" unless specifically requested.
3. CSS Design Tokens:
   - Never use arbitrary hardcoded colors for themed surfaces. Always use CSS custom 
     properties: var(--bg-color), var(--surface-color), var(--primary-color), 
     var(--accent-gold), var(--text-primary), var(--text-secondary), var(--border-color).
4. Dual Navbar Awareness:
   - Navbar styles in Navbar.css are split between .navbar-horizontal and .navbar-vertical. 
     Modifications to navbar items must account for both horizontal desktop layout and 
     vertical floating left dock layout.
5. Intro Scrollytelling Protection:
   - FrameScrollIntro.jsx manages body scroll locking and high-DPI canvas drawing. 
     Any changes to total frames must update TOTAL_FRAMES constant (currently 300) 
     and the frame URL generator.
